1
00:00:04,069 --> 00:00:12,139
The man known to history as Nikola Tesla was
born on the 10th of July 1856 in Smiljan,

2
00:00:12,139 --> 00:00:19,890
Lika, which was originally part of the Austro-Hungarian
empire but is now located in Croatia.

3
00:00:19,890 --> 00:00:26,070
His father was Milutin Tesla, a priest of
the Serbian Orthodox Church and the son of

4
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:32,070
Nikola Tesla’s grandfather who was also
named Nikola. His grandfather had served as

5
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:37,640
a military officer for the French Empire during
the Napoleonic Wars and had risen to the rank

6
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:44,719
of sergeant, before marrying Tesla’s grandmother
Ana Kalinic, the daughter of a respected colonel.

7
00:00:44,719 --> 00:00:49,790
Following the defeat of Napoleon, Nikola Tesla
returned to Lika, which was assimilated into

8
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:55,840
the Austro-Hungarian empire, where he fathered
two sons including Milutin and his brother

9
00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:02,450
Josif, as well as 3 daughters named Stanka,
Janja, and another whose name is unknown.

10
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:07,909
Milutin Tesla and his brother were sent to
the Austrian Military Officer’s Training

11
00:01:07,909 --> 00:01:13,259
Academy to follow the career path of their
father, and while Josif thrived, eventually

12
00:01:13,259 --> 00:01:18,900
becoming a professor of Mathematics at a military
academy in Austria where he authored several

13
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:26,079
standard mathematical textbooks, Milutin decided
instead to choose a devotional path, enrolling

14
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:33,380
in the Orthodox Seminary in Plaski to train
as a priest after being castigated in training

15
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:39,409
for not maintaining the shininess of his brass
buttons. Nikola Tesla’s mother was Djuka

16
00:01:39,409 --> 00:01:46,010
Mandic, the daughter of a priest from Gracac
called Nikola Mandic, and the sister to three

17
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:51,630
very successful brothers including Nikolai,
who climbed the ecclesiastical ranks to become

18
00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:58,009
the Archbishop of Sarajevo and the Metropolitan
of the Serbian Orthodox Church in Bosnia,

19
00:01:58,009 --> 00:02:04,290
Pajo who became a colonel in the general staff
of the Austrian army, and finally Trifun who

20
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:09,750
excelled in the business sphere as a respected
hotelier and landowner. In addition to being

21
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:16,790
a dedicated housewife, Djuka Mandic possessed
a keen intellect and a strong work ethic and

22
00:02:16,790 --> 00:02:22,209
was herself an innovator of her household
appliances which she often modified to make

23
00:02:22,209 --> 00:02:28,010
more efficient. She was “An inventor of
the first order” according to Tesla and

24
00:02:28,010 --> 00:02:32,970
a creative influence on him until her death
in 1892.

25
00:02:32,970 --> 00:02:41,599
Milutin Tesla was a gifted student and graduated
with top honors in 1845, marrying the 25-year-old

26
00:02:41,599 --> 00:02:48,790
Djuka Mandic in 1847 after being delegated
to oversee the parish of Senj on the Adriatic

27
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:54,659
Coast. Settling into a house perched on top
of a cliff overlooking the ocean, the newlyweds

28
00:02:54,659 --> 00:03:01,770
started a family, with Djuka giving birth
to their eldest son Dane in 1848, a firstborn

29
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:09,910
daughter Angelina in 1850, and finally another
daughter Milka in 1852. However due to the

30
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:15,360
poor pay he received and the salty sea air
which caused him health problems, Milutin

31
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:22,470
Tesla was reassigned to the Church of St Apostles
Peter and Paul in Smiljan, which meant “the

32
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:28,430
place of sweet basil”, in Lika province,
where he was provided with a picturesque farmhouse,

33
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:35,340
a parcel of fertile land, and even an Arabian
horse so that he could ride to see his parishioners,

34
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:41,769
it was given to him by a Turkish pasha based
in Bosnia as a reward for assisting some local

35
00:03:41,769 --> 00:03:47,909
Muslims. As well as being an extremely smart
man who assembled a vast library packed full

36
00:03:47,909 --> 00:03:54,360
of volumes on religion, mathematics, science,
and literary works in many different tongues,

37
00:03:54,360 --> 00:04:01,140
Milutin Tesla was also an arduous reformer
of the Serbian people, regularly writing articles

38
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:06,810
for a variety of newspapers and tirelessly
promoting the establishment of language schools

39
00:04:06,810 --> 00:04:11,209
where Serbians could learn to read and write.

40
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:16,370
According to his family, Nikola Tesla was
born at midnight sometime between the ninth

41
00:04:16,370 --> 00:04:23,139
and tenth of July 1856 in the middle of a
terrific thunderstorm. Three days later Nikola

42
00:04:23,139 --> 00:04:29,180
was baptized at his family home, and with
his future seemingly already planned, he was

43
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:35,740
also enlisted as a member of the First Lika
Regiment of the Ninth Medak Company, a squadron

44
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:41,500
he was to join when he was 15 years old by
law. By all accounts, Tesla’s childhood

45
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:47,630
was happy, and one he shared with his older
siblings as well as his younger sister Marica,

46
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:53,229
born in 1859, who would often accompany him
to the churchyard or the farmyard to play

47
00:04:53,229 --> 00:04:59,139
with the chickens, geese, sheep and other
livestock which his father kept. Tesla was

48
00:04:59,139 --> 00:05:05,230
often joined by his black cat Macak, who first
introduced him to the phenomenon that would

49
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:11,580
define his life’s work after he set off
a loud spark upon stroking him, an event which

50
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:17,800
was explained by his father as a secretion
of electricity. In another formative experience

51
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:24,190
again involving Macak, Tesla noted one day
how a halo of light suddenly surrounded his

52
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:30,860
dear cat, illuminating briefly, the candlelit
room he was sitting in. Inspired by such marvels,

53
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:37,229
Tesla devoted much of his energy as a child
to experimenting and encouraged by his mother’s

54
00:05:37,229 --> 00:05:42,080
inventive streak, drew up plans for flying
machines very similar to how a helicopter

55
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:47,550
would later function, he disassembled clocks
to see how they worked, and even designed

56
00:05:47,550 --> 00:05:54,020
himself a wooden sword so that he could pretend
to be a valiant Serbian warrior. Behind the

57
00:05:54,020 --> 00:06:00,199
fascination however lay a troubled young mind,
as Tesla revealed that as a young boy, he

58
00:06:00,199 --> 00:06:05,660
suffered from a strange affliction whereby
he couldn’t distinguish images from reality

59
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:11,370
which troubled him greatly. Tesla’s childhood
trauma was exacerbated by the death of his

60
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:17,620
older brother Dane in 1863, who was killed
in front of Tesla by the family’s Arabian

61
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:23,520
horse in a traumatic experience that would
endlessly haunt him, and which was also the

62
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:29,699
reason why his distraught father moved his
family from the idyllic Croatian countryside

63
00:06:29,699 --> 00:06:35,729
to the larger town of Gospić, an unfamiliar
environment where Tesla struggled to adjust

64
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:37,800
to urban living.

65
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:43,800
The untimely passing of Dane cast a long shadow
over Tesla’s own relationship with his father

66
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:50,449
who, mired in grief, always under appreciated
the talents of his youngest son, a neglect

67
00:06:50,449 --> 00:06:55,870
that young Nikola tried to compensate for,
by striving to be perfect in everything he

68
00:06:55,870 --> 00:07:03,050
did so that he could win back the love of
his parents. Blinded by sorrow, Milutin Tesla

69
00:07:03,050 --> 00:07:08,400
treated his young son with contempt, flying
into rages when he caught him reading from

70
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:14,819
his private library, and on one particularly
hurtful occasion, after Nikola had accidentally

71
00:07:14,819 --> 00:07:21,320
ruined a local noblewomen’s dress by unintentionally
jumping on it as it trailed down the aisle

72
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:27,819
of a church, he slapped his son across the
face in public as a punishment. As a result

73
00:07:27,819 --> 00:07:34,319
of his strained relations, Tesla developed
a series of peculiar phobias as a child, such

74
00:07:34,319 --> 00:07:40,930
as a repulsion for women who wore earrings
and pearls, a strong aversion to hair, a loathing

75
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:46,900
for the smell of camphor, as well as a number
of other strange habits, including an obsession

76
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:53,150
with counting his steps and measuring in volume
the contents of his meals, calculations he

77
00:07:53,150 --> 00:07:59,830
was only satisfied with if they were divisible
by three. Overwhelmed by a plethora of odd

78
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:06,010
neuroses, Tesla was able to regain some sense
of balance after he came across a novel called

79
00:08:06,010 --> 00:08:13,830
Abafi, published in 1836 by Hungarian author
Miklós Jósika, which featured the story

80
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:20,490
of Olivér Abafi, a young impulsive nobleman
and hedonist, recast as a valiant national

81
00:08:20,490 --> 00:08:27,280
hero who sacrifices himself for the wellbeing
of the country. Tesla was particularly inspired

82
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:33,159
by the character of the protagonist, seeing
in his desire to better his moral character

83
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:39,640
while ignoring frivolous distractions, a masterful
example of self-restraint, which showed Tesla

84
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:45,960
that it was indeed possible for him to control
his wild emotions. Tesla realized that a good

85
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:51,620
coping strategy was to work with, rather than
against, the nebulous visions that assaulted

86
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:57,670
his consciousness, and delving even deeper
into the make-believe world of his imagining,

87
00:08:57,670 --> 00:09:02,950
Tesla began to embark on strange journeys
where he would stumble across fantastical

88
00:09:02,950 --> 00:09:06,350
countries, people, and cities that he dreamed
up.

89
00:09:06,350 --> 00:09:13,720
As Tesla honed that untamed imagination that
would later serve him so well in his profession,

90
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:19,300
he began theorizing about the nature of reality
itself, coming to the conclusion, that he

91
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:25,790
could trace all of his mental images back
to something he either saw, smelt, or touched,

92
00:09:25,790 --> 00:09:31,480
in an early echoe of the mechanistic view
of the world he would later espouse. It was

93
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:37,829
also an idea that had real-life application
for Tesla, who on one occasion was extolled

94
00:09:37,829 --> 00:09:44,649
as a hero by a band of firemen after he spotted
a small kink in a fire hose he instinctively

95
00:09:44,649 --> 00:09:49,959
knew was preventing water from reaching a
burning building, a problem he quickly fixed

96
00:09:49,959 --> 00:09:56,459
by ironing the groove out. Tesla’s ingenuity
would be further fostered at the Real Gymnasium,

97
00:09:56,459 --> 00:10:02,029
the grammar school he attended in Gospić,
where he would amaze his mathematics professors

98
00:10:02,029 --> 00:10:08,910
by demonstrating a natural ability to calculate
numbers, but while he excelled in scientific

99
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:15,070
pursuits, Tesla was unable to translate his
talents to drawing class, where a preference

100
00:10:15,070 --> 00:10:22,300
for undisturbed contemplation distracted Tesla
heavily, leading to grades that were so extremely

101
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:28,160
poor, his father had to speak with the principal,
which instilled in a young Nikola a lifelong

102
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:31,329
aversion to diagrams.

103
00:10:31,329 --> 00:10:37,600
During his schooling at the Real Gymnasium
Tesla began to take invention seriously, devising

104
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:44,440
the schematics for a flying machine that would
use the pressure of a vacuum to push air molecules,

105
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:50,390
a concept that a grown-up Tesla would later
go on to disprove. Shortly after he graduated

106
00:10:50,390 --> 00:10:57,310
from the Real Gymnasium in 1870 Tesla, perhaps
because of his overactive imagination, became

107
00:10:57,310 --> 00:11:03,139
very sick with a range of maladies sufficiently
serious enough for the doctors treating him

108
00:11:03,139 --> 00:11:10,690
to nearly give up on his case entirely. Throughout
his recuperation Tesla began voraciously reading,

109
00:11:10,690 --> 00:11:16,089
and it was during this period that he was
first introduced to the tales of Mark Twain.

110
00:11:16,089 --> 00:11:21,950
It was a story he would later recount to Mark
Twain himself, who burst into tears upon hearing

111
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:28,310
it. After a period of convalescence, Nikola
Tesla was next enrolled at the higher Real

112
00:11:28,310 --> 00:11:36,360
Gymnasium in Karlovac in 1873 where, in accordance
with his father’s wish for Tesla to continue

113
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:42,889
the family profession, he was enlisted in
classes at the local seminary. However, Tesla’s

114
00:11:42,889 --> 00:11:48,880
true desire was to learn everything he could
about electricity, a passion ignited by an

115
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:54,620
inspirational physics teacher who taught him
about the radiometer invented by British scientist

116
00:11:54,620 --> 00:12:00,829
William Crookes, a device that powered a vacuum
bulb with energy produced by four rapidly

117
00:12:00,829 --> 00:12:07,240
spinning tinfoil vanes, this roused Tesla
to conduct some of his first experiments with

118
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:13,570
batteries, induction coils, and electro-static
generators. Yet Tesla would have to put some

119
00:12:13,570 --> 00:12:19,880
of his projects on hold after again falling
seriously ill with cholera upon his return

120
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:26,740
home to Gospić, causing the young prodigy
to be bedridden for over 9 months and to experience

121
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:32,990
several close shaves with death. After one
particularly worrying incident, Tesla supposedly

122
00:12:32,990 --> 00:12:39,040
implored his father that if he were to study
engineering instead of entering the priesthood

123
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:44,279
that he may well recover causing Milutin,
desperate to avoid the unbearable pain of

124
00:12:44,279 --> 00:12:50,750
losing another son, to solemnly promise that
Nikola would go to the best technical institution

125
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:53,089
in the world.

126
00:12:53,089 --> 00:12:59,720
Having finally been heard, Tesla made a miraculous
recovery, but before he could become a student

127
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:04,850
he was sent to the Croatian mountains with
nothing but a bundle of books and some hunting

128
00:13:04,850 --> 00:13:10,420
equipment by his father who, worried for his
son’s health, did everything in his power

129
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:16,660
to hide his son from the authorities, as by
law, Tesla would have to serve in the Austrian

130
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:23,750
armed forces for 3 years. For nine months
starting in the early fall of 1874, Tesla

131
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:29,380
wandered the forests and lakes of the eastern
European countryside, becoming stronger physically

132
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:35,820
and mentally as he thought deeply about invention,
reshaping the vividness of his visions from

133
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:42,300
a debilitating weakness into a powerful contemplative
tool that could be used to flesh out the contraptions

134
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:48,160
that flashed across his mind, such as a pipe
installed underwater that could transport

135
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:53,980
letters and packages placed in capsules using
the principles of hydraulic pressure, and

136
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:59,450
a ring constructed around the earth’s equator
that could be used as a high-tech transport

137
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:01,170
network.

138
00:14:01,170 --> 00:14:06,449
When Tesla returned, his father had kept his
promise, securing for him a scholarship at

139
00:14:06,449 --> 00:14:12,639
the Military Frontier Administration Authority
that would enable him to study for three years

140
00:14:12,639 --> 00:14:19,170
at the Polytechnic School in Graz, Austria.
Receiving an embroidered bag made from typical

141
00:14:19,170 --> 00:14:26,660
Serbian materials from his mother which he
would always prize, in 1875 Tesla left Gospić

142
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:32,300
to start anew in a completely different culture
and environment, in the same way that his

143
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:39,240
own Serbian relatives had adapted to life
on the Austro-Hungarian border decades prior.

144
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:45,019
During his freshman year, Tesla proved himself
to be a perfect student, never once missing

145
00:14:45,019 --> 00:14:52,110
a lecture and supposedly studying from 3am
to 7pm every day, a schedule that was thought

146
00:14:52,110 --> 00:14:57,970
so extreme that one professor wrote to Milutin
warning him that unless his son was escorted

147
00:14:57,970 --> 00:15:03,699
out of the school, that he might work himself
to death, while others commended him for his

148
00:15:03,699 --> 00:15:09,290
zeal, such as the Dean of the Technical Faculty
who informed Milutin Tesla that his son was

149
00:15:09,290 --> 00:15:13,279
quote: “a star of first rank.”

150
00:15:13,279 --> 00:15:19,410
In fact, Tesla was keeping himself very busy,
administering his earliest experiments with

151
00:15:19,410 --> 00:15:25,660
alternating current or ‘AC’ that would
later make his name, but during his sophomore

152
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:31,709
year Tesla would be sidetracked, developing
a destructive gambling habit and wagering

153
00:15:31,709 --> 00:15:38,329
away his entire tuition fund in the process.
Near destitute, Tesla had also neglected his

154
00:15:38,329 --> 00:15:45,170
studies, scoring extremely poorly in the examinations,
and with no marks registered for his final

155
00:15:45,170 --> 00:15:51,269
semester, he was also unable to graduate and
was forced to abandon the university in December

156
00:15:51,269 --> 00:15:58,770
1878, a failure he made sure to keep secret
from his family as well as his classmates,

157
00:15:58,770 --> 00:16:06,259
as he was riddled with guilt and embarrassment.
In 1879, Tesla would live for a while in self-imposed

158
00:16:06,259 --> 00:16:12,490
exile, first making his way to the city of
Maribor where he became a draughtsman and

159
00:16:12,490 --> 00:16:18,870
was paid 60 florins a month, while in his
free time he continued to play cards and wager

160
00:16:18,870 --> 00:16:25,339
money on the streets with the locals, yet
Tesla’s Slovenian sojourn would be short-lived,

161
00:16:25,339 --> 00:16:30,300
as a couple of months into his stay, he was
seized by the authorities for not possessing

162
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:36,790
a proper residency permit and returned to
Gospić escorted by armed police. Back home

163
00:16:36,790 --> 00:16:43,040
Tesla’s father would not get much time to
set his son straight, as only a month later,

164
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:51,579
on the 17th of April 1879, Milutin died, heartbroken
that his son had been labelled as a ‘vagrant’

165
00:16:51,579 --> 00:16:57,730
and had chosen to indulge in a life of vice.
Not content to see their talented nephew waste

166
00:16:57,730 --> 00:17:04,660
his abilities, in January 1880 two of Tesla’s
uncles gave him enough money to start courses

167
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:11,920
at the Charles-Ferdinand University in Prague,
despite Tesla not meeting the language requirement,

168
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:18,371
which specified that students had to be fluent
in both Czech and Greek. However, communication

169
00:17:18,371 --> 00:17:25,140
issues aside, he also arrived too late, and
was unable to enroll in classes, and so for

170
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:32,890
the entire time Tesla was only permitted to
attend lectures and received no formal grades.

171
00:17:32,890 --> 00:17:39,600
In 1881 Nikola Tesla landed his first job
for a telecommunications firm in Budapest

172
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:45,789
called The American Telephone Company, where
he was drafted in as an electrical engineer

173
00:17:45,789 --> 00:17:52,140
by Tivador Puskas, who had previously worked
alongside Thomas Edison, the inventor of the

174
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:58,420
lightbulb, at the Edison laboratories in Menlo
Park. Making himself a valuable employee and

175
00:17:58,420 --> 00:18:04,390
sharing his findings with his work colleague
Anital Szigety, Tesla continued his study

176
00:18:04,390 --> 00:18:10,159
of the concept of the alternate current in
his spare time, proposing that a motor driven

177
00:18:10,159 --> 00:18:17,140
by circuits that were out of phase could maintain
power levels to supply a constant stream of

178
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:22,250
electricity, but in order to make the system
function, Tesla realized he needed to figure

179
00:18:22,250 --> 00:18:28,750
out how to rotate magnetic fields. Strolling
in the park with Anital Szigety in February

180
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:36,580
1882, Tesla had a sudden stroke of genius
and solved the rotating magnetic field problem,

181
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:42,929
going on to explain the concept of the induction
motor to his friend by drawing its basic blueprints

182
00:18:42,929 --> 00:18:49,100
in the sand with a stick, outlining a new
type of engine that unlike its Direct Current

183
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:55,950
or ‘DC’ counterpart, did not need a commutator,
an inefficient cylindrical device segmented

184
00:18:55,950 --> 00:19:03,290
with metal that had to be regularly maintained.
Impressed by Tesla’s genius, Tivador Puskas

185
00:19:03,290 --> 00:19:08,679
recommended that Tesla move to Paris to work
for his old acquaintance Thomas Edison at

186
00:19:08,679 --> 00:19:14,140
his Continental Edison Company, a firm that
specialized in electrical equipment, where

187
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:19,179
he was first assigned by his boss Charles
Batchelor, a manager who had worked for Edison

188
00:19:19,179 --> 00:19:26,650
since 1870, with designing dynamos, a contraption
that converted mechanical energy into electrical

189
00:19:26,650 --> 00:19:32,880
energy and which was used most commonly in
direct-current circuits. Off the clock however,

190
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:39,980
Tesla continued to advance the AC theory after
he was sent to work on a project in Strasbourg,

191
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:43,679
where he built the first induction motor prototype.

192
00:19:43,679 --> 00:19:50,800
However, Tesla was unable to garner any serious
interest in Alternating Currents. This was

193
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:56,770
unfortunate, as alternating current is recognized
today as a better method of electric current

194
00:19:56,770 --> 00:20:02,010
delivery than direct current. Direct current,
of the kind which came to dominate electricity

195
00:20:02,010 --> 00:20:07,850
delivery systems in the late nineteenth century,
consistently sends electricity in one direction

196
00:20:07,850 --> 00:20:13,690
along an electric grid. Alternating current,
by way of contrast, periodically reverses

197
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:21,090
and changes direction along a grid or system
as its magnitude alternately reverses course.

198
00:20:21,090 --> 00:20:26,110
Alternating current is considerably more efficient
than direct current. Tesla’s error, if it

199
00:20:26,110 --> 00:20:31,950
can be defined as such, is that he was simply
ahead of his time in trying to propose alternating

200
00:20:31,950 --> 00:20:38,190
current as the better method of energy generation.
He was correct, but the technology available

201
00:20:38,190 --> 00:20:43,970
at the time simply favoured the more crude
direct current method. Tesla soon found himself

202
00:20:43,970 --> 00:20:50,270
in another personal finance crisis after spending
all of his wages, yet he had done enough during

203
00:20:50,270 --> 00:20:55,830
his stint at the company to impress his overseer
Charles Batchelor, who was convinced that

204
00:20:55,830 --> 00:21:02,570
Tesla had the intellectual fortitude to work
alongside Thomas Edison himself.

205
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:08,480
In 1884, after being mistakenly registered
as a migrant from Sweden after the immigration

206
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:14,510
officer misheard him say ‘Smiljan’, Nikola
Tesla arrived in America armed with an introductory

207
00:21:14,510 --> 00:21:21,320
letter penned by his mentor Charles Batchelor,
