00:31:20,570 --> 00:31:27,380
at Madison Square Gardens, where he demonstrated
a radio-controlled boat he called a Telautomaton,

307
00:31:27,380 --> 00:31:33,789
to stunned audiences, and by 1901 he had been
awarded with a patent clarifying that he had

308
00:31:33,789 --> 00:31:38,840
created a system for transmitting electrical
energy.

309
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:45,409
Between 1899 and 1900, after being commissioned
by John Jacob Astor to assemble a new lighting

310
00:31:45,409 --> 00:31:51,490
system in a contract worth 100,000 dollars,
Tesla relocated his laboratory at Colorado

311
00:31:51,490 --> 00:31:57,480
Springs where, disobeying his patron’s instructions
completely, he decided instead to explore

312
00:31:57,480 --> 00:32:02,500
‘terrestrial stationary waves’, which
he regarded as his greatest discovery. At

313
00:32:02,500 --> 00:32:08,570
this rural outpost located far away from the
humdrum of New York City, Tesla started to

314
00:32:08,570 --> 00:32:14,279
piece together an enormous transmitter powered
